{"t_ms": 3915453, "conversation_id": "conv_sentence_end_s4_011", "turn_id": 1, "actor": "system", "event_type": "retrieval_result", "payload": {"passages": ["Deluxe Room Information\n\nGrand Horizon Hotel & Suites\n\nThe Deluxe Room offers a comfortable stay with a king-size bed, air conditioning, a smart TV, complimentary Wi-Fi, tea and coffee-making facilities, and a work desk. Each room includes an attached bathroom with premium toiletries and a hairdryer. The room accommodates up to two adults and one child. Daily housekeeping is included in the room rate.", "Indoor Games Room\n\nGrand Horizon Hotel & Suites\n\nGuests can enjoy a variety of indoor recreational activities including table tennis, carrom, chess, billiards, and board games. The Games Room is open daily from 8:00 AM to 10:00 PM. Equipment should be returned after use, and guests are requested to maintain a quiet and respectful environment.", "# corpus/ \u2014 Hotel Documents\n\n**Owner: Lakshya**\n\n## What this folder is\n\nThe hotel's documents live here: the knowledge the assistant answers from. About 60 short \ndocuments covering things like pool and gym hours, check-in and check-out rules, menus, and \npolicies.\n\n## How to fill it\n\nSee the full instructions in `retrieval/README.md` (Step 1). In short:\n- Write ~60 short documents, one topic per file, as `.txt` or `.md`.\n- Make them realistic and varied.\n- Deliberately plant a few contradictions (e.g. one doc says the pool closes at 10 PM, \n  another says 9 PM) and keep a note of which ones, for a later experiment.\n\nThe index-building script reads every file in this folder, so anything you put here becomes \npart of the searchable knowledge.\n"], "scores": [0.4325520992279053, 0.6615227460861206, 0.6701545715332031], "timing_policy": "sentence_end", "timing_trigger": "sentence_end", "user_end_known_at_finish": true, "launch_offset_ms_vs_user_end": 1344, "overlap_with_speech_ms": 0, "forecast_invalidated": false}}
